MiBench basic math
==================

Part of A653_Benchmarks: classic WCET (worst-case execution time) kernels run
as periodic ARINC 653 processes, to measure their execution time under JetOS.
Each period the process runs the kernel once; with GET_STAT enabled
(BenchmarksTools/benc_config.h) it also prints the execution time and the
running WCET, BCET and ACET.

What it tests
-------------

Execution time of a heavy floating-point workload with a lot of console output.

What it does
------------

One partition, P1, with one periodic process.

Runs the MiBench "basicmath" program: solves cubic equations, computes integer
square roots (usqrt) and converts angles between degrees and radians. The
"large" data set runs in a process with a 1 s period and a hard 1 s deadline.

Expected output
---------------

Lines starting with "Solutions:", "sqrt(...)" and angle conversions; about 9500
lines per second in QEMU.

Notes
-----

In QEMU the large data set takes longer than its 1 s budget (mostly because of
the console output), so the hard deadline is missed and the HM table restarts
the partition ("Restarting partition P1 due to: Deadline Missed"). Set
OUTPUT_ENABLED to 0 or use the small data set to stay within the budget.

Origin
------

Ported from MiBench 1.0 (http://vhosts.eecs.umich.edu/mibench/).

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/A653_Benchmarks/MIB_Basicmath/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/A653_Benchmarks/MIB_Basicmath/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
